# ==============================================================================
# fish-shell: Red Hat System-wide Configuration Template
# ==============================================================================
# This template configures system-wide settings for the fish shell on Red Hat
# based distributions. It serves as the base configuration loaded by all fish
# instances, unless overridden by user-specific configs in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fish.
#
# Directory structure for overrides:
# - System-wide: /etc/fish/config.fish (this file)
# - User-specific: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fish/config.fish
# - Drop-in snippets: /etc/fish/conf.d/*.fish
# - User drop-ins: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fish/conf.d/*.fish
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Variable: xdg_config_home
# Description: The XDG_CONFIG_HOME environment variable, typically used to determine
#              the user configuration directory path.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If XDG_CONFIG_HOME is not set, fish defaults to $HOME/.config.
# This variable reference allows users to customize the path if needed.
{% set xdg_config_home_val = xdg_config_home | default('$XDG_CONFIG_HOME') %}

# The path to the user's configuration directory.
# Note: In fish, this is often handled by the shell itself, but we document
# the intended override path here for clarity.
# set -g XDG_CONFIG_HOME {{ xdg_config_home_val }}

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# General Behavior
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is executed by every fish instance.
# Use `status` commands to conditionally apply settings for login or interactive shells.

# Example: Settings only for login shells
# if status is-login
#     # Add custom login paths here
# end

# Example: Settings only for interactive shells
# if status is-interactive
#     # Add interactive prompts or colors here
# end

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Configuration Snippets Directory (conf.d)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# To include modular configuration, place .fish files in the system conf.d directory:
#    /etc/fish/conf.d/*.fish
#
# Users can override these snippets by placing files with the same name in their
# local conf.d directory:
#    {{ xdg_config_home_val }}/fish/conf.d/*.fish
#
# The system conf.d files are loaded first. User files in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fish/conf.d
# are loaded later, allowing users to override or extend system settings.

# Note: No default system-wide commands are inserted here to allow flexibility.
# Administrators should add specific system-wide commands (e.g., PATH modifications)
# directly to this file or via conf.d snippets.
